    "growth_rate_source": "judgment: equity_5yr_cagr 5.7% tempered toward mid-single-digit industry growth; all trailing CAGRs span the COVID boom (FY21-22) and bust plus the Sep-2023 Veralto spin, so none is a clean run-rate",
    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity 5y CAGR 5.7% vs revenue 5y 2.0% and EPS 5y 0.4% (and 3y revenue -2.7%, EPS -19.7%): divergence >30%. Causes: COVID testing/bioprocess peak in FY21-22 then destocking, Veralto spin-off (Sep-2023) removing ~$5bn of revenue, Abcam acquisition (Dec-2023). Equity growth reflects retained earnings and FX, not organic growth.",
    "notes": "Owner-FCF series (reported FCF - SBC - equity-award taxes; no interest-income strip as DHR is net-debt): FY2020 5,172, FY2022 7,007, FY2025 4,893. SBC-adjusted and reported FCF CAGRs are close (SBC ~1.2% of revenue), so SBC is not driving the gap; the decline is the post-COVID normalisation plus the Veralto spin."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Mid-single-digit core growth after a soft FY26 (3-4% core guide, respiratory headwind ~250bp in Q3-26, ~$100m bioprocess revenue into 2027), full-year Masimo from the close, and DBS lifting Masimo's lower margin so group pre-SBC EBITDA reaches ~32.5% by year 4.",
    "bull": "Bioprocessing recovery runs to double-digit, Cytiva resin share (~80%) and validated-workflow lock-in hold price, Masimo becomes a genuine second Diagnostics growth platform, and margins expand toward ~34.5% - a return to the DBS compounding record.",
    "bear": "A second bioprocess destocking leg, China VBP pricing, the respiratory roll-off and a stalled Masimo integration during the CEO handover keep growth at 2.5-3.5% and margins flat at ~30%; the market stops paying a compounder multiple (16x exit cap)."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "House basis values Danaher on unlevered owner FCF with SBC and equity-award withholding fully expensed, share count held flat, and the post-Masimo balance sheet deducted. The revenue base is pro forma for a full year of Masimo so the acquisition debt and the acquired flows are matched. Acquired-intangible amortisation is kept out of both the tax base and the cash flows; the cash tax rate is calibrated to EBITA from actual cash taxes paid.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Terminal value is roughly two-thirds of EV; the 20x cap binds near Gordon at 8.2%/3.0%, so exit-multiple assumptions dominate",
      "Masimo annualised revenue (~$2.2bn) and margin are estimates until the Q3-26 10-Q discloses the post-close contribution",
      "Bioprocess destocking recurrence (the axis between base and bear)",
      "StatLab acquisition not modelled (cost and flows both excluded)",
      "Metrics.csv TotalDebt for Q1/Q2 2026 double-counts current debt; the DCF uses the XBRL LongTermDebt total instead"
    ]
  },
