    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Risk-free 4.3% (10y UST), ERP 5.0%, beta ~0.9 -> cost of equity ~8.8%; pre-tax cost of debt ~4.6% (-> ~3.6% after tax) at ~12% debt weight on market values (net debt 22.2bn vs market cap ~159bn) -> WACC ~8.2%. One WACC across all scenarios: risk is carried in the scenario paths and weights, not a premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP operating leases (~$1.3bn liability): lease cost is already inside operating expense and therefore inside EBITDA; lease liabilities are NOT added to net debt. lease_cost_pct_path = 0 to avoid a second charge.",
    "nci_treatment": "Noncontrolling interest $11m at 2026-06-26 - immaterial, ignored.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build (dcf-methods routing row 'operating company'). Danaher is a life-sciences tools / bioprocessing / diagnostics operating company with a recurring consumables base; none of the bank/REIT/holdco rows apply. First valuation of DHR (no MEMORY entry). US filer: owner-fcf-adaptations not required (USD flows and quote, US GAAP operating leases inside EBITDA, SBC-positive market).\n\nFY0 AND MASIMO: Masimo closed 2026-06-10 for $9.84bn cash (XBRL PaymentsToAcquireBusinessesNetOfCashAcquired H1-26). The net debt anchor is the 2026-06-26 balance sheet, which already carries the acquisition debt; so the revenue base must carry Masimo too, or the model would pay for Masimo without owning its flows. base_revenue = TTM Jun-26 revenue 25,107 (FY25 24,568 + H1-26 12,216 - H1-25 11,677) - ~95 of Masimo stub already booked + ~2,200 annualised Masimo continuing (healthcare, post consumer-audio sale) revenue = ~27,200. The Masimo run-rate is an estimate; replace with disclosed figures from the Q3-26 10-Q. Year 1 of the projection is Jul-26 to Jun-27.\n\nNET DEBT: LongTermDebt (total incl. current portion) 26,558 at 2026-06-26 (noncurrent 25,147 + current 1,411) less cash, cash equivalents and restricted cash 4,348 = 22,210. DATA ISSUE: Metrics.csv TotalDebt for Q1 2026 (19,407) and Q2 2026 (27,969) equals LongTermDebt PLUS DebtCurrent, i.e. double-counts the current portion (27,969 = 26,558 + 1,411); FY2025 18,420 is correct. Should be fixed via make fix. Metrics.csv also has no CashAndEquivalents after FY2019 (XBRL tag changed to CashCashEquivalentsRestrictedCash...).\n\nOWNER FCF: reported FCF TTM 5,466 (OCF - capex) - SBC incl. equity-award taxes 366 = 5,100. Interest income NOT stripped: DHR is net-debt (the H1-26 interest income of 88 was earned on cash pre-funded for Masimo and is gone). Reported FCF is after cash interest paid; the DCF is unlevered and deducts net debt instead, so the valuation flows are built from EBITDA, not from last_fcf.\n\nCOMPONENTS: EBITDA margin is pre-SBC GAAP EBITDA: FY25 op income 4,690 + depreciation 750 + amortisation 1,697 + SBC 298 = 7,435 (30.3%, depressed by impairment/restructuring); H1-26 2,471 + 389 + 897 + 151 = 3,908 (32.0%). Masimo dilutes ~0.5pp at close (Diagnostics margin -160bp in Q2). D&A path is DEPRECIATION ONLY (~3.1-3.2% of revenue); acquired-intangible amortisation is non-cash and excluded from both the tax base and the add-back, and the cash tax rate is calibrated to EBITA accordingly: cash taxes paid FY25 1,200 / EBITA (4,690 + 1,697) 6,387 = 18.8%; FY24 1,300 / ~6,400 = ~20%. Capex FY23-25 5.8%/5.8%/4.7%, H1-26 4.1%. Working capital negative capture (manufacturer/distributor: receivables + inventory exceed payables) at -15% of the revenue increase.\n\nBUYBACKS: DHR is an active repurchaser (FY24 5,979; FY25 3,088; H1-26 894) - the flat count is funded, not just a modelling convention. Dividends ~0.9bn/yr are a use of owner FCF, not a deduction.\n\nNOT MODELLED: StatLab (announced, expected to close by YE26; price undisclosed in the inputs available) - neither its cost nor its flows are in the model. Pension deficit and legal reserves not bridged (immaterial vs a ~$180bn EV).",
